  "id": "transplantation",
  "term": "transplantation",
  "definition": "In this source, transplantation refers to moving stage performance language into film with relatively little change, so visible theatrical conventions are kept on screen. This direct carryover may preserve the stage feel, but it can reduce narrative flow and emotional coherence for audiences.",
